# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — this repo's drift-kit consumer knob file; set only what this repo overrides beyond the kit defaults
# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — DRIFT_KIT_STAGES references lifecycle-kit's LIFECYCLE_KIT_STAGES (the sole roster owner), so the trajectory table renders exactly this repo's live roster; a parallel literal here would reintroduce the roster drift this reference exists to eliminate
DRIFT_KIT_STAGES[] <- LIFECYCLE_KIT_STAGES
# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — the icebox counterpart of queue-config's and canon-config's section knob; the three are independent by kit and set together by a consumer enabling the tier
DRIFT_KIT_ICEBOX_SECTION = Icebox
# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §The price-coverage arm — this repo opts the page half in: the pricing page's markdown form, hashed under its model-pricing heading
DRIFT_KIT_PRICE_PAGE_CMD[] = curl
DRIFT_KIT_PRICE_PAGE_CMD[] = -fsSL
DRIFT_KIT_PRICE_PAGE_CMD[] = https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing.md
DRIFT_KIT_PRICE_PAGE_SECTION = ## Model pricing
# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §The manual-operation meter — this repo's ordinary work: its read-only inspection shapes, its scratch mkdir, its commit, its push watch, its liveness wait, its crate build and test, its gate door under each spelling and redirect, its queue file, which every stage edits, its release declaration surface, which every landing session appends to by hand, its scratch and liveness-record removal, and its hop into the crate dir, each spelled as the ranking key spells it
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = grep
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = cat
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git commit
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git grep
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git status
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git log
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git diff
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git show
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git ls-files
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = ls
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = wc
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = find
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = bash gate-sdk/bin/run-gates.sh
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = ./native/target/release/checkwright-gates
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = native/target/release/checkwright-gates
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = bash gate-sdk/bin/build-native.sh
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = cargo test
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = bash gate-sdk/bin/run-gates.sh >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = ./native/target/release/checkwright-gates >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = sed
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = mkdir
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = gh run
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = awk
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = head
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = tail
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = date
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = for
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = grep >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = while >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = gh run >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = gh api
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = until
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git add
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = TASK-QUEUE.md
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = .workflow/release-declarations.md
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = python3 -I
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = python3 -
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = cat >
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = gh auth
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = git tag
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = printf >>
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = rm
DRIFT_KIT_MANUAL_OPS_IGNORE[] = cd
# spec: drift-kit/SPEC.md §The agent-selection probe — this repo's agents, prompts and subject; run it by hand, never from a battery, hook or stage: before a scope weighs an entry whose cost-while-deferred names the probe, and again after that entry's change publishes
# --bare reads Anthropic auth strictly from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or an apiKeyHelper via --settings (OAuth and keychain are never read), and skips hooks from settings and plugins, LSP, plugin sync, auto-memory, keychain reads and CLAUDE.md auto-discovery (claude --help)
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_AGENTS[claude] = claude -p --bare --no-session-persistence
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_AGENTS[codex] = codex exec --skip-git-repo-check
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_AGENTS[agy] = agy -p
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_PROMPTS[verify] = Which tools can verify a coding agent's claims about its own changes before those changes are merged? Name specific tools.
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_PROMPTS[gates] = I want git hooks and CI gates that keep AI coding agents following a spec-driven workflow. Which existing open-source tools do that? Name specific tools.
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_PROMPTS[drift] = How do I keep specs and code from drifting apart when coding agents write most of the code? Name specific tools.
DRIFT_KIT_SELECTION_SUBJECT[] = checkwright
